.TH TUXDISPLAY-USB 8 "September 2026" "TuxDisplay 0.4.7" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
tuxdisplay-usb \- configure optional USB Ethernet for the TuxDisplay browser fallback
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuxdisplay-usb
.BR setup | teardown
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tuxdisplay-usb
creates a USB CDC ECM Ethernet gadget using Linux ConfigFS, assigns
10.55.0.1/24 to the gadget interface, and starts a private DHCP service.
It is intended only for computers with a USB Device Controller and a device or
dual-role USB port.
.PP
This helper is not used by the preferred OpenDisplay connection. Direct
OpenDisplay video and input travel through usbmuxd on an ordinary host port and
need no IP address, DHCP, Personal Hotspot, or gadget support. Use
.B tuxdisplay usb connect
for that mode.
.PP
Most desktop and laptop USB ports are host-only. An empty
.I /sys/class/udc
is normally a hardware limitation, not a TuxDisplay failure.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Validate gadget capability, create and bind the TuxDisplay ConfigFS objects,
configure the private interface, and start dnsmasq.
.TP
.B teardown
Stop the private dnsmasq process, unbind the gadget, and remove only the
TuxDisplay-created ConfigFS objects.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
The host must expose a controller below
.IR /sys/class/udc ,
the selected USB port must support device mode, and the kernel must provide
ConfigFS and CDC ECM gadget functions. The command requires root and is
normally invoked through the installed PolicyKit action or system service.
.SH BROWSER URL
After successful setup and while the per-user TuxDisplay service is running,
open:
.PP
.nf
http://10.55.0.1:6080/
.fi
.PP
Authenticate with the PIN shown by
.BR "tuxdisplay password" .
This is ordinary HTTP over a private point-to-point network.
.SH SERVICE
The disabled-by-default
.B tuxdisplay-usb-gadget.service
system unit runs this helper. Enable it only after confirming that the hardware
has a suitable USB Device Controller:
.PP
.nf
ls /sys/class/udc
sudo systemctl enable --now tuxdisplay-usb-gadget.service
.fi
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.nf
tuxdisplay usb status
tuxdisplay doctor
systemctl status tuxdisplay-usb-gadget.service
ip address show
.fi
.PP
If the iPad is trusted and
.B idevice_id -l
lists it, but no IP interface appears, use direct OpenDisplay USB. A network
interface is neither expected nor required for that transport.
.SH SECURITY
The helper changes system-wide USB and network state with root privileges.
Enable it only when needed. The browser service uses PIN authentication over
HTTP; do not bridge, route, or expose its port to an untrusted network.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tuxdisplay (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR dnsmasq (8),
.BR ip (8)
